WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
- This is considered the
most right wing government

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.690
in Israel's history,

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:06.480
led by Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.310
This is the National Security Minister.

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:10.800
He was once convicted
of incitement to racism

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.350
and belonging to a terrorist organization.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:15.180
And this is the Finance Minister.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:18.420
He's advocated for permanent
Israeli rule over the West Bank

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.910
without giving Palestinians
the right to vote.

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:23.430
Many of these politicians
are strongly in favor

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:26.580
of the judicial overhaul plan
that sparked massive protests

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:28.800
and created a rift with allies.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:30.930
- They cannot continue down this road.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:33.750
- Well, Netanyahu now says
he wants to seek compromise,

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:35.790
he needs to keep the
support of his coalition

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:37.200
in order to stay in power.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:40.140
So here's how Netanyahu came
to be politically reliant

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.810
on religious and ultranationalist parties

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:44.580
and why the interests of his government

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:47.913
are now clashing with many of
Israel's citizens and allies.

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:50.760
Before we talk about
the judicial overhaul,

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:53.430
let's talk about how
Netanyahu came back into power

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:54.483
in the first place.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:56.670
Just a few years ago,

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:59.010
it looked like his political
career might be over.

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:02.640
In 2019, he was indicted on
bribery and fraud charges,

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:03.840
which he denies.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:04.980
And in 2021,

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:08.040
his rivals agreed to form a
new government to oust him.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:10.169
But Netanyahu didn't back down.

00:01:10.169 --> 00:01:13.982
(speaking foreign languages)

00:01:13.982 --> 00:01:16.380
He fought the charges, and even
though he was still on trial

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:18.960
during the campaign, he
pulled off an election victory

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:21.270
by uniting right wing, ultranationalist,

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:23.193
and religiously conservative parties.

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:27.330
That opened the door for
people like Itamar Ben-Gvir,

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:29.040
leader of the Jewish Power Party,

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.133
to secure top government positions.

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:34.800
(speaking foreign language)

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:37.740
Politicians in Netanyahu's
government support

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.660
all kinds of divisive policies,

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:41.520
but one of their biggest priorities

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:43.740
is to overhaul the
country's judicial system

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:46.380
so that they as politicians can override

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:49.200
Supreme Court decisions
that they don't agree with.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:52.800
So why is this judicial overhaul
such a big deal to them?

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:55.530
Unlike in the US and some
other Western countries,

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:58.170
Israel doesn't have a
written constitution.

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:00.720
Judges are picked by a
judicial selection committee,

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:01.920
not politicians,

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.560
and they base their decisions
on British common law,

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:08.340
evolving Israeli precedent,
and a series of basic laws.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.380
Supporters of this system say it provides

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.570
checks and balances against parliament.

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:15.450
But for decades, Israel's right
wing has accused the court

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:17.400
of having a left wing bias.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.320
For example, most Israelis are subject

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.150
to mandatory military service,

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:24.350
but many in Netanyahu's government
want Ultra-Orthodox Jews

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:25.830
to be exempt from it,

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:28.200
so that they can study
Jewish texts full-time.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:30.720
But when Parliament passed a
law on that a few years ago,

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:34.470
the court struck it down
saying it was unconstitutional.

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:36.150
So fast forward to January,

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:38.490
when Netanyahu and his allies took power,

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:41.640
they put out proposals to
completely change the system

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.920
like giving lawmakers
power on the committee

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:46.830
that appoints judges, making
it easier for Parliament

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:48.780
to overrule Supreme Court decisions,

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:51.270
and making it harder for
judges to strike down

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:52.410
Parliament's Laws.

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:55.380
The proposals set off a wave of protests

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:57.210
with demonstrators saying the overhaul

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.520
would weaken Israel's checks and balances.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:03.933
- This is emergency time
for the democracy of Israel.

00:03:05.329 --> 00:03:08.010
- [Shelby] Crucially,
scores of Israeli reservists

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:11.160
said they would refuse to
serve if the reforms passed.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:12.150
On the other side,

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:14.970
supporters of the proposals
also demonstrated,

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:17.321
demanding that the proposals move forward.

00:03:17.321 --> 00:03:20.988
(speaking foreign language)

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:27.000
- And they were cheered on by
some in Netanyahu's cabinet,

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.850
who tweeted videos and thanked
them for their support.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:32.880
With flights grounded,
schools shut and banks closed,

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:35.730
Netanyahu pressed pause
and his coalition agreed

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:38.100
to suspend some of the
more contentious issues

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:39.792
until after Passover.

00:03:39.792 --> 00:03:43.459
(speaking foreign language)

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:48.099
But the showdown is far from over.

00:03:48.099 --> 00:03:52.200
(speaking foreign language)

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.630
Some in Netanyahu's
Coalition are still vowing

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:56.400
to press ahead with the reforms.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.950
At the same time, Netanyahu
is facing pressure

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:01.830
from Israeli citizens who
continue to demonstrate,

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:03.240
and the United States,

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:05.824
which is Israel's
largest security partner.

00:04:05.824 --> 00:04:09.307
- Like many strong supporters
of Israel, I'm very concerned.

00:04:09.307 --> 00:04:10.140
- [Shelby] Netanyahu responded,

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:12.120
saying Israel is a sovereign country

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.730
which makes its decisions
by the will of its people

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.740
and not based on pressures from abroad,

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:18.630
including from the best of friends.

00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:21.270
Now, analysts say if
Netanyahu really wants

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:22.440
to reach a consensus,

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:24.330
he'll have to give
members of his coalition

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.470
something in return.

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:27.690
Already he has agreed to give Ben-Gvir,

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:30.210
the National Security
Minister, even more power,

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:32.880
by handing him control
of the National Guard,

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:35.010
a move that would put the Ultranationalist

00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:37.438
in charge of handling protests.

00:04:37.438 --> 00:04:40.021
(gentle music)

